scope one whole unsent lap recovered and landed, four peer conflicts derived rather than chosen, four witnesses re-proven on metal, one instrument finding handed to Copal
status GREEN on named guards, and the FULL ROSTER DID NOT CLOSE -- said plainly rather than implied. The hot pass reached 11 of roughly 217 guards in 22 minutes, all green, on a pier carrying four concurrent roster passes at load 12.3, so a full pass here projects to about seven hours and cannot ride a lap. Proven instead by running each guard this lap bears on, directly, at this HEAD: link_counted, readme_metrics, ascii_document, living_pin_near_bound, index_row_bound, session_roster_agree, tracked_link, shell_dialect, instrument_refusal and tame_style_check, plus e123_living_pin_guard and exec_bit inside the pass. Twelve green, zero red. The REDS pin stands at its bound with all 16 rows OPEN, so this lap's finding is recorded on the card rather than booked -- a raise or a fold is Keaton's word.
recommend keep-going -- the latency is measured at 13s and the repair is one line of the refusal: print the lock's age and whether a signal has already landed, so a hand can tell a pending stop from an ignored one. Next lap builds that reading and proves it from both sides in a pen.
